rom the $x$-axis. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "627918cc-4b21-5f54-b208-cb86d8a90fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238922} {:answer/id #uuid "9f41d10b-f851-5d45-9827-61f7b022fc29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239445} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e51c7e-db29-5f2f-8366-bcfa0cafd1d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239898} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb49dbb-7200-53b3-81d0-14d6d6fcc22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239981} {:answer/id #uuid "e21e0841-2d32-541f-bd4e-00d6bca599f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f41d10b-f851-5d45-9827-61f7b022fc29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239445} :answer-field/id #uuid "116238d5-19f2-50cb-9748-dd30cea9d39a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240357}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2172851-a396-51c3-bd4e-4e1278b37143" :question/math-academy-id "q-105575" :question/problem "![](images/11/11d38951b884f17616a61403d793322d0e2ea28910e806fe8f018251508352a1.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nI. $∇\\cdot F=0$\n\nII. $∇\\cdot F>0$\n\nIII. $∇\\cdot F<0$\n\nIV. $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36de03da-2578-5f05-876f-f54a0a9294f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238529} {:answer/id #uuid "7aaa08fe-4d2a-57c5-86e7-f6781940e81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239113} {:answer/id #uuid "80cdae6e-5c8b-5697-89ab-7480fc566987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239174} {:answer/id #uuid "9056720e-3c5f-5cf9-a8ee-fb59548a6f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239308} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b392bc-be27-5e13-8e38-e3b0402b8388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aaa08fe-4d2a-57c5-86e7-f6781940e81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I an