omain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move horizontally and vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336f3f9e-6053-5a86-b639-96673bb8f672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257234} {:answer/id #uuid "39162a94-0d90-5b25-b209-24876a170a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257285} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8b15ca-d52d-531a-9f40-45fe63da8575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257571} {:answer/id #uuid "5c64bab9-76fe-5d95-8daf-e8e1b620127c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257585} {:answer/id #uuid "a0382c8f-1bdd-5f43-bb7f-8f4cbd016ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39162a94-0d90-5b25-b209-24876a170a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257285} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0c79f3-5071-5ae2-996b-25bb19951a62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d890a9be-d244-5a2b-a434-390b31123a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-123245" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b315be9ba524ab538388fdaad31161c280d7d6e5ab71261345063ac6ffe819d5.png)\n\nCon