er is \"II and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "231945f5-5ce3-591d-8c60-6a81b26bce4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238364} {:answer/id #uuid "5cde9981-76e2-5111-b3d2-8d4bb59f9102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238866} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd04a75-4a7b-5127-a5de-42010f421aa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238890} {:answer/id #uuid "e2dd249f-7c15-560d-becc-a4d5d9208c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240051} {:answer/id #uuid "f786ef25-6354-54b3-81ae-fc54056ba558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fd04a75-4a7b-5127-a5de-42010f421aa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238890} :answer-field/id #uuid "5159a419-7fd4-51ac-aa59-e88ebd5af8fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240479}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dbe3e81-bcac-55ba-b175-6059759ab5dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105695" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cc62b0a51519230bd1230874c00e17f165c345d11bc64e6d3c8fcf7788a5ee8.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- $F$ is not irrotational\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into from the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35c1aead-eb9d-582c-b0d6-f68d1170a78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263474} {:answer/id #uuid "6af6b5a3-6222-5cfd-8bca-6b4614394bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263920} {:answer/id #uuid "716bd08d-5f1f-5c82-bf30-535c8d7dc64c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263980} {:answer/id #uuid "b2edc390-c4fb-5a29-a137-faed40c674b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :an